From b8466b056ad06422b5b89e85ae64a0efd533eddd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Rabert <ar@nullsum.net>
Date: Sat, 20 Dec 2025 18:28:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] vo_libmpv: add Vulkan support to gpu-next backend

Add Vulkan support to the gpu-next libmpv render backend, allowing
applications to use mpv with their own Vulkan device. This mirrors
the existing OpenGL API but for Vulkan.

New public header render_vk.h defines:
- mpv_vulkan_init_params: device import parameters
- mpv_vulkan_fbo: per-frame render target
- mpv_vulkan_sync: optional semaphore synchronization

The implementation uses libplacebo's pl_vulkan_import to import the
user's VkDevice rather than creating a new one. Users must enable
required Vulkan 1.2 features (hostQueryReset, timelineSemaphore) when
creating their device.

Per-frame rendering wraps user-provided VkImages via pl_vulkan_wrap
and properly releases them to libplacebo before rendering.
